# Which field reads are read from the place itself (panel 215's R3, ratified
# 2026-10-16; design.md §4.8): `p.n` lowered as one `load` of the place `p.n`,
# `(*p).f_n` in C, where it was a `load` of the whole `p` into a temporary and
# a field of that copy. § 9 says the callee works on the caller's place
# itself, and the copy made it false of the emitted C at `-O0`: a record
# holding a lock was copied, lock and all, to read one field (the sitting's
# critic, § 4). The same held of a local cell, which C may hold the address
# of too, so every place is read so, a parameter's and a local's alike.
#
# A path of fields alone, rooted in a local or a parameter, each field found
# on its record: an index keeps its own instruction and its bound check, and
# a module's name, a constant, a call or any other value is not a place.
#
# **And never a read whose value is a fixed array.** C gives a `T[N]` no
# storage, so the emitter spells such a value where it is used
# (`emit/storageless.hero`): read in place, it would read the place at its
# use rather than at the read, after any write between them, `f(x.b,
# g(@x))` handing `f` the array `g` wrote. Found at this landing, when the
# first build of it left fifteen programs naming a temporary nothing
# declared, exit 2; such a read keeps the whole value's read and the field
# of that copy, whose spelling `storageless.hero` knows.

use ast
use source
use resolved
use check/state
use check/table
use ir/layout

# Whether `id` is a field read through a path of fields alone, rooted in a
# local or a parameter, each field found: the read `place` spells whole.
function read(a: ast.Ast, r: resolved.Resolved, c: state.Checked, s: source.Source, decls: [ast.Decl], id: i64) -> bool
    match a.exprs[id].kind
        .name =>
            match r.uses[id]
                .local                                  => return true
                .top | .builtin | .module | .unresolved => return false
        .field f =>
            match table.get(c.types, c.expr_types[id])
                .fixed                                                    => return false
                .int_ty | .float_ty | .bool | .str | .ptr | .cstr | .unit => _ = 0
                .array | .map | .fallible | .function_ty | .named         => _ = 0
                .case_ty | .failure | .generic | .error                   => _ = 0

            match r.uses[f.base]
                .module                                => return false
                .local | .top | .builtin | .unresolved => _ = 0

            if layout.field_index(decls, c, s, owner: c.expr_types[f.base], name: f.name).is_err()
                return false
            return read(a, r, c, s, decls, id: f.base)
        .field_name | .index | .int_lit | .float_lit | .str_lit | .interp | .char_lit => return false
        .bool_lit | .null_ptr | .hole | .unary | .binary | .call | .method            => return false
        .variant_case | .array | .map | .try_expr | .if_expr | .match_expr | .error   => return false

    return false
